#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""pairdeck (PairDeck): animated HTML explainer decks, a comment loop on the slides, and a visual-style guide that learns.

The agent builds a deck with the bundled engine (`pairdeck new`), checks every slide on screenshots (`pairdeck qa`) and
records its version (`pairdeck snapshot`). The author opens the deck in the local review page (`pairdeck review`), drags a box
on a slide and types a comment. `pairdeck watch` waits for comments and for the author's own edits to the deck files, lets them
settle, prints one batch and exits; that exit wakes the agent that started it in the background. The agent fixes the deck,
answers each comment (`pairdeck resolve`, shown under the comment on the review page), snapshots again, learns from the
evidence (`pairdeck learn`), and starts `pairdeck watch` again.

`pairdeck seed` reads the author's past decks (.pptx, .pdf, .html) through ../shared/seed_visual.py, so the style guide starts
close to the author's taste.

Data (profile, style vault, projects) lives in $PAIRDECK_HOME, else ~/.pairdeck (`pairdeck setup`). `pairdeck paths` prints
where. Standard library only (Python 3.9+), plus git for the data home and Chrome or Chromium for screenshots (`CHROME=`).
"""

from __future__ import annotations

